  "details": "Create some form of whitelisting user created coding content.  In a game that has a community so invested in creating content for itself, coding development should not be excluded.\nAfter a mod has been whitelisted, add it to a browsing system.  Creators can add a title,  description, and category (locomotion, QoL, accessibility, performance, IK, etc.) of their mod and what it does.  They can then be chosen by users to be locally implemented.  Creators are given the option to remove their mods at any point, just like any other content, but they must be reevaluated to be uploaded back to the game.",
